# Flutter + GetX Architecture (Sayes-style)

Use this stack: **Flutter**, **GetX** (routing, DI, state), **Dio** (HTTP), **shared_preferences**. Follow clean layering and the conventions below.

## Folder layout

```
lib/
  main.dart
  app/
    bindings/          # {Feature}Binding — registers controllers
    routes/routes.dart # Routes constants + GetPage list
    use_cases/         # {Domain}UseCase — orchestrates repositories
    translations/      # AppTranslations extends Translations
    utils/constants.dart
  data/
    preferences/       # PrefsManager — static prefs helpers
    remote/
      dio_client.dart    # GetxService, single Dio instance
      dummy/             # dummy JSON + RemotePost helper (DataSource layer only)
        dummy_json.dart
        remote_post.dart
      data_sources/      # {Domain}DataSource — HTTP or dummy JSON
    repositories/        # {Domain}RepositoryImpl — parse JSON only
  domain/
    models/
      beans/             # {Entity}Bean — domain/DTO models
      responses/         # {Entity}Response extends BaseResponse
    repositories/        # abstract {Domain}Repository
  presentation/
    base/base_controller.dart
    screens/{feature}/
      controller.dart
      screen.dart
      widgets/           # screen-specific widgets (not shared across screens)
    widgets/             # shared UI (e.g. AppButton)
```

## Naming

| Kind | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Screen file/class | `screen.dart` / `{Feature}Screen` | `welcome/screen.dart` → `WelcomeScreen` |
| Controller | `controller.dart` / `{Feature}Controller` | `WelcomeController` |
| Binding | `{feature}_binding.dart` / `{Feature}Binding` | `WelcomeBinding` |
| Use case | `{domain}_use_case.dart` / `{Domain}UseCase` | `AuthUseCase`, `ProductsUseCase`, `ShopsUseCase` |
| Repository (abstract) | `{domain}_repository.dart` | `AuthRepository` |
| Repository impl | `{domain}_repository_impl.dart` | `AuthRepositoryImpl` |
| Data source | `{domain}_data_source.dart` | `AuthDataSource` |
| Entity model | `{entity}_bean.dart` / `{Entity}Bean` | `GarageBean` |
| API model | `{entity}_response.dart` / `{Entity}Response` | `GaragesResponse` |
| Screen widget file | `widgets/{name}.dart` / `{Name}` | `home/widgets/product_card.dart` → `ProductCard` |
| Route constant | camelCase path | `static const String signIn = "/signIn";` |
| API methods | `request` prefix | `requestProfile()`, `requestGarages()` |
| Private fields | `_camelCase` | `final AuthUseCase _authUseCase` |

Use `package:{app_name}/...` imports (replace `{app_name}` with the pubspec `name`).

## Dependency injection (GetX)

- **main**: `Get.put(DioClient(), permanent: true)` after `PrefsManager.init()`.
- **Binding**: `Get.lazyPut(() => FeatureController())` in `dependencies()`.
- **Use case**: `Get.put(RepositoryImpl())` on the repository field.
- **Controller**: `Get.put(UseCase())` on use-case fields; extend `BaseController`.
- **Data source**: `Get.find<DioClient>()` (hide Get's `Response` when importing Dio).

## Data flow

```
Controller → UseCase → Repository (abstract) → RepositoryImpl → DataSource → DioClient
```

- **DataSource**: `post(path, variables: map)` → return `response.data` as `Map<String, dynamic>`.
- **RepositoryImpl**: call data source, `return XxxResponse.fromJson(json)`.
- **UseCase**: thin delegate — one-liner `=> _repository.requestXxx(...)`.
- **Controller**: never call repository or Dio directly. Never import dummy JSON helpers outside the data layer.

## Dummy JSON (until real endpoints)

Use dummy API-shaped JSON in the **DataSource** layer until backend endpoints are provided.

- **`Constants.useRemoteApi`**: `false` (default) → DataSource returns dummy JSON from `DummyJson`. Set to `true` when endpoints are ready.
- **`lib/data/remote/dummy/dummy_json.dart`**: static maps matching real API shape (`statusCode`, `data`, `message`).
- **`RemotePost`**: wraps `DioClient.post`; when `useRemoteApi` is `false` returns `dummyJson`; when `true` calls Dio and falls back to `dummyJson` on failure.
- **DataSource** methods pass `dummyJson: DummyJson.xxx()` into `RemotePost.post(...)`.
- **RepositoryImpl**: only `fromJson` — no dummy/fallback logic.

```dart
// products_data_source.dart
Future<Map<String, dynamic>> requestProducts() => _remote.post(
  Constants.productsPath,
  dummyJson: DummyJson.products(),
);

// products_repository_impl.dart
Future<ProductsResponse> requestProducts() async {
  final json = await _productsDataSource.requestProducts();
  return ProductsResponse.fromJson(json);
}
```

When endpoints are ready: set `Constants.useRemoteApi = true` and update paths in `Constants` if needed. Controllers and repositories stay unchanged.

## Domain modules

Group use cases, repositories, and data sources by domain. Prefer fewer, cohesive modules:

| Module | Repository / DataSource | UseCase | Responsibility |
|--------|----------------------|---------|----------------|
| **Auth** | `AuthRepository`, `AuthDataSource` | `AuthUseCase` | Sign in/up, password reset, verification, logout, **profile** |
| **Products** | `ProductsRepository`, `ProductsDataSource` | `ProductsUseCase` | Products list, featured, details, favorites |
| **Shops** | `ShopsRepository`, `ShopsDataSource` | `ShopsUseCase` | Shops list, shop details, shop products |
| **Cart** | `CartRepository`, `CartDataSource` | `CartUseCase` | Cart, checkout |
| **Order** | `OrderRepository`, `OrderDataSource` | `OrderUseCase` | Orders, details, track, return |
| **Settings** | `SettingsRepository`, `SettingsDataSource` | `SettingsUseCase` | About us, terms, contact us |

Do **not** create separate Profile, Catalog, Content, Contact, or App modules — fold them into the modules above.

## Screen ↔ UseCase mapping

Every screen controller with data or actions must wire to a suitable use case:

| UseCase | Screens |
|---------|---------|
| `AuthUseCase` | Sign In, Sign Up, Forget Password, Verification, Reset Password, Edit Profile, Settings (logout) |
| `ProductsUseCase` | Home, Products, Product Details, Favorites |
| `ShopsUseCase` | Shops, Shop Details |
| `CartUseCase` | Cart |
| `OrderUseCase` | Orders, Order Details, Order Track, Order Return |
| `SettingsUseCase` | About Us, Terms, Contact Us |

Navigation-only screens (e.g. Splash, No Internet, Server Error) may omit a use case.

## BaseController & API calls

Every controller extends `BaseController`. Use shared loading and error handling:

```dart
Future<void> requestProfile() async {
  isLoading.value = true;
  final response = await _authUseCase.requestProfile();
  isLoading.value = false;
  if (!isSuccess(response)) return;
  // handle success
}
```

- `isSuccess(response)` checks `statusCode == 200`; failures go through `onApiError`.
- `statusCode == -1` → navigate to no-internet route; `-2` → server-error route.
- Other errors → `Get.rawSnackbar` with `response.message` or `'warning'.tr`.

Load initial data in `onInit()` → `super.onInit()` then call `request*()` methods.

## Models

- **BaseResponse**: `message`, `statusCode`, `isSuccess` (`statusCode == 200`), `fromJson` factory.
- **Responses** extend `BaseResponse`, pass `json` to `super`, parse `data` in `fromJson`.
- **Beans**: immutable-style fields, `const` constructor, `factory fromJson`.

## Routing

- All routes in `Routes` class + `List<GetPage> routes` in `app/routes/routes.dart`.
- Each `GetPage`: `name`, `page: () => const XxxScreen()`, `binding: XxxBinding()`.
- Navigation: `Get.toNamed`, `Get.offNamed` (replace stack). Pass retry context via `arguments` map keys `"currentRoute"` and `"arguments"`.

## UI

- Screens: `class XxxScreen extends GetView<XxxController>` with `const` constructor and `super.key`.
- Access controller via `controller` (from `GetView`) — e.g. `controller.navigate`.
- User-visible strings: **`.tr`** keys in `AppTranslations` (`en` / `ar`).
- Primary actions: reuse **`AppButton`** (`text`, `onPressed`, optional `isLoading`, optional `gradient` / `backgroundColor`).
- Full-width pill buttons (`borderRadius: 32`, height 56), solid `AppColors.primary` by default.
- Text fields: reuse **`AppTextField`** (`hint`, optional `prefixIconPath` for SVG icons, `suffixIcon`).
- Common layout: `Scaffold` → `SafeArea` / `Container` with `DecorationImage` background → `Padding(24)`.
- Prefer `const` widgets where possible; `StatelessWidget` for shared widgets.

### Screen-specific widgets

- **Do not** define private widget classes (`_Foo`) or widget-builder methods (`Widget _buildFoo()`) inside `screen.dart`.
- Any widget used only by one screen lives in that screen's `widgets/` folder:

```
presentation/screens/home/
  screen.dart
  controller.dart
  widgets/
    product_card.dart   → ProductCard
```

- Import with `package:{app_name}/presentation/screens/{feature}/widgets/{file}.dart`.
- Reusable across multiple screens → `presentation/widgets/` instead.
- `screen.dart` should mostly compose child widgets and bind to the controller.

### Design assets & icons

When implementing UI from a design (Figma, screenshot, etc.):

- Match layout, spacing, colors (`AppColors`), and typography as closely as possible.
- If a screen uses a **custom icon** (logo, branded glyph, etc.) that cannot be reproduced accurately with Flutter `Icons` or simple shapes, add a placeholder **SVG** under `assets/icons/` (e.g. `ic_logo.svg`, `ic_email.svg`).
- Register assets in `pubspec.yaml` (`assets/icons/`). Load with `flutter_svg` and reference paths from `AppIcons` in `lib/app/utils/app_icons.dart`.
- Add a short comment in the SVG file: `<!-- Placeholder: replace from Figma export -->`.
- **Tell the user** which SVG files need to be replaced with exact exports from Figma.
- Do not embed one-off icons inline in `screen.dart`; keep them as assets or screen `widgets/`.

## HTTP (DioClient)

- Single `DioClient extends GetxService`; all endpoints use **`post`** (even reads).
- `validateStatus: (_) => true`; map connection failures to `statusCode: -1`, other errors to `-2`.
- Request body key: `variables` in `post(query, variables: {...})`.

## Preferences

- `PrefsManager` static API: `init()`, getters/setters using `Constants` keys, `clear()` on logout.

## Style

- `flutter_lints` defaults; no unnecessary comments.
- Empty controllers are only acceptable for pure navigation screens (no data, no API).
- Match existing file naming: **snake_case** files, **PascalCase** types.
- Do not introduce new state libraries (Bloc, Riverpod, Provider) unless asked.
- Keep screens thin; business logic and API calls live in controllers and below.
